## Outcomes

- SQLite/libsql, DynoStore, and SlateDB initialize epoch 0 and record a new epoch boundary when a produced batch has a greater `partition_leader_epoch`.
- Repeated and lower produced epochs do not add duplicate history entries.
- Lite `SemaphoreProxy` now forwards `leader_epoch_history`, so service code sees real storage history.
- Fetch stale/future epoch tests now create epoch 1 through storage produce instead of raw SQL.
- API 23 remains routed but unadvertised.
- Storage epoch, storage ListOffsets, broker Fetch, compatibility contract, and all-features check passed.

## Residual Risks

- Broker ListOffsets wire-level tests fail for mixed-partition error and produced-epoch cases with `KafkaProtocol(Message("overflow"))` or `UnexpectedEof`; direct storage ListOffsets proof passes.
- API 23 is still unadvertised pending differential/client proof.
- Leader epoch truncation/recovery and read-committed transaction integration remain unproven.
